{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>He will cut down.</b> In the sense of cutting off." "<b>The tangled forest.</b> The intertwined trees." "<b>With iron.</b> A parable for an angel." "<b>[And Lebanon with a mighty one shall fall].</b> And the officers, who are like the trees of Lebanon, shall fall by mighty iron. Now 'with iron' draws itself and another along with it."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:20.594911256Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}